{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## The fix direction is DEMONSTRATED, with an honest caveat\n\nRe-ran the same 9 files with a private slot directory — `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR=$(mktemp -d)`, so\nthe run gets its own `locks/` and its own 4 slots — while the four host-global slots stayed\noccupied by the other sessions listed in the description:\n\n```\n116 passed, 2 errors in 993.46s (0:16:33)\n```\n\n**Zero `GateCongestedError`.** Compare the same 9 files minutes earlier against the shared\nhost slot directory: `14 failed, 102 passed`, every failure `all 4 concurrent slots busy`.\nOne environment variable is the whole difference, which is as clean a confirmation of the\nmechanism as this is going to get.\n\n### The 2 errors are mine, not the suite's\n\n```\nERROR tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py::test_code_change_reruns_full_review\n  - Failed: The repo HEAD moved during this test (25d1d683e5 -> 8b2fee219f)\nERROR tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py::test_agentic_case_reroots_injected_runner_at_its_fixture\n  - Failed: The repo HEAD moved during this test (8b2fee219f -> 38396ebfcc)\n```\n\nThose two SHAs are my own commit and my own `make amend-msg`, run in that worktree while this\nverification was still in flight. The suite has a guard for exactly that and it fired\ncorrectly. So: not gate congestion, not a test defect, and not evidence for or against this\nticket — operator error on my part, recorded here rather than quietly dropped, because a\nreader comparing \"116 passed, 2 errors\" against my \"zero failures\" claim deserves to know\nwhich two and why.\n\nIt is also the second time in one session that acting on the tree during a long run polluted\nthe run. Cheap lesson, stated for the record: do not commit, amend, or edit inside a worktree\nthat has a suite running in it.\n\n### What this implies for the fix\n\nThe change needed is at the FIXTURE level, not in `gate_admission`: point `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR`\nat a per-session temp dir for the test suite. Production semantics stay exactly as they are —\na real gate op on a real host should contend for a genuinely shared, host-wide semaphore,\nwhich is the whole point of the design. Only the tests need to stop borrowing it.\n\n### Relationship to `torrential-unwhite-snail` (9c2e-b44c-119e-4105)\n\nRead that ticket before assuming this one supersedes it — it does not, and I want the record\nstraight rather than flattering. 9c2e already frames the cause cross-session (\"Any other\nsession on the machine holding gate slots — another agent running `review-plan` or a\ncompletion-gated close\"), and it already asks, in its own AC4, for \"a check that no other test\nin the suite has the same host-wide coupling, or a ticket filed for any that do\".\n\nSo this ticket is not a correction of 9c2e. It is the **answer to its AC4**, plus three things\n9c2e left open:\n\n1. the concrete code path (`_slot_dir()` -> `store_root()/locks` -> `tempfile.gettempdir()`),\n2. the scale (31 tests, 9 files, not 1), and\n3. the reason ordinary triage misleads here — admission fails closed WITHOUT waiting, so\n   re-running a test alone does not isolate it, and the holders can be processes running no\n   tests at all.\n\nIf anything is superseded it is the instinct to treat these as one-off flakes; the coupling is\nstructural and this is its inventory."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788590283526986001,"uuid":"3d38cc66-c82b-4a1d-9f9b-f642a3329ca0"}